# Kskin CMS regression

- One Chrome/browser, one login; one module at a time.
- ACTIVE↔INACTIVE only on QA-created items (Gift Card singleton exception).
- Actions first: inspect listing/detail before automating; soft-fails → Failed.
- View-only → listing/search/pagination only (no invented edit).

## QA confidence (skip vs manual)

Framework under `qa-confidence/` — not another pass/fail suite.

- Invoke with **`/QA_ConfidenceWorkflow`** (skill `QA_ConfidenceWorkflow`).
- Read `qa-confidence/README.md` + `qa-confidence/prompts/agent_guardrails.md`.
- Prefer cheapest CMS layer from `qa-confidence/trust_policy.yaml`.
- Update scenario/case YAML after work; regenerate via `scripts/generate_qa_confidence_report.py`.
- Never claim `trusted` with open caveats; `_example_*` is demo only.

Handoff: `reports/REGRESSION_PROGRESS.md`.
